  cursor: pointer;
}
```

list-style: none se bullet gayab. Menu aksar list se banta hai, wahan ye hamesha lagta hai.

```css
ul {
  list-style: none;
  padding: 0;
}
```

overflow: hidden bahar nikalne wale hisse ko kaat deta hai. scroll lagane se andar hi scroll aa jata hai.

```css
.dabba {
  width: 200px;
  height: 100px;
  overflow: hidden;
}
```

Teeno tareeke ke selector: p = saare paragraph, .khaas = class walon ke liye (dot lagta hai), #title = sirf us ek id wale ke liye (hash lagta hai).

```css
p { color: blue; }
.khaas { color: red; }
#title { color: green; }
```

ID wala niyam jeetega. CSS me takat ka order hai: id sabse takatwar, phir class, phir aam element selector. Isiliye is example me hara rang lagega:

```css
#title {
  color: green;
}
```

Chhote page ke liye internal CSS chal jata hai. Style tag hamesha head ke andar rakho.

```html
<head>
<style>
  p {
    color: blue;
  }
</style>
</head>
```

CSS me comment /* aur */ ke beech likhte hain. Bade file me ye batane ke kaam aata hai ki kaunsa style kis hisse ka hai.

```css
/* Ye note hai: neeche heading ka style hai */
h1 {
  color: navy;
}
```

outline: none se purani outline hat ti hai. Par kuch apna nishaan (jaise hari border) zaroor do, warna user ko pata nahi chalega dabba chuna gaya hai.

```css
input:focus {
  outline: none;
  border: 2px solid green;
}
```

HTML me class="card bada" likhne se dono class ke niyam ek saath lag jate hain. Ek class sajawat ke liye, dusri size ke liye — aise CSS reuse hota hai:

```css
