let se variable banta hai. Naam ko " " (quotes) ke andar likhte hain kyunki ye text (string) hai. console.log se browser ke console me dikhta hai.

```javascript
let naam = "Vishesh";
console.log(naam);
```

const wala variable ek baar set hone ke baad badla nahi ja sakta. Janm tithi, naam jaisi pakki cheezon ke liye const use karo.

```javascript
const umar = 20;
console.log(umar);
```

var purana tareeka hai, let naya. Aaj kal let aur const hi use hote hain — var me kuch purani gadbadiyan hain jo bade code me pareshani deti hain.

```javascript
var purana = 10;
let naya = 20;
console.log(purana + naya);
```

Number par quotes nahi lagte. Quotes laga doge to wo text ban jayega aur jod ki jagah jud jayega (4991 jaisa galat jawab).

```javascript
let daam = 499;
console.log(daam + 1);
```

Do text ko + se jodte hain. Beech me " " (khaali jagah) jodna mat bhoolna, warna naam chipak jayega.

```javascript
