console.log(jawab);
```

Console browser me F12 dabakar khulta hai. Code ki galti dhundhne (debugging) me console.log sabse bada saathi hai.

```javascript
console.log("Ye mera pehla message hai");
console.log("Jod:", 10 + 20);
```

Button ke onclick me function ka naam likho. Click hote hi wo function chalega. Function ko script tag me banate hain.

```html
<button onclick="namaste()">Dabao</button>
<script>
function namaste() {
  alert("Namaste Boss!");
}
</script>
```

getElementById se wo element pakdo jiski id msg hai, phir innerText badal do. Yehi JavaScript ka sabse kaam ka pattern hai.

```html
<p id="msg">Purana text</p>
<button onclick="badlo()">Text Badlo</button>
<script>
function badlo() {
  document.getElementById("msg").innerText = "Naya text aa gaya!";
}
</script>
```

Element ki style badalne ke liye .style ke baad CSS wali property likhte hain. Dhyaan do — JS me background-color ko backgroundColor likhte hain.

```html
<h1 id="title">Meri Heading</h1>
<button onclick="rangBadlo()">Rang Badlo</button>
<script>
function rangBadlo() {
  document.getElementById("title").style.color = "red";
}
</script>
```

Photo badalna matlab img ki src badal dena. Nayi photo ka naam src me dalte hi browser use load kar deta hai.

```html
<img id="photo" src="din.jpg" width="200">
<button onclick="raat()">Raat Karo</button>
<script>
function raat() {
  document.getElementById("photo").src = "raat.jpg";
}
</script>
```

Pehle halat jaancho: chhupa hai to dikhao, dikh raha hai to chhupao. Isi ko toggle kehte hain.

```html
<div id="dabba">Ye chhupa hua khazana hai</div>
<button onclick="toggle()">Dikhao/Chhupao</button>
<script>
function toggle() {
  let d = document.getElementById("dabba");
  if (d.style.display === "none") {
    d.style.display = "block";
  } else {
    d.style.display = "none";
  }
}
</script>
```

Double click ke liye ondblclick event hota hai. Aam click ke liye onclick, do baar tez dabane ke liye ondblclick.

```html
<img src="photo.jpg" width="150" ondblclick="bada()">
<script>
function bada() {
  alert("Photo par double click hua!");
}
</script>
```

return false dene se form asal me bheja nahi jata aur page refresh nahi hota. Ye jaanch (validation) ke liye pehla kadam hai.

```html
<form onsubmit="return bhejo()">
<input type="text" id="naam">
<input type="submit" value="Bhejo">
</form>
