<button onclick="ghatao()">-</button>
<script>
let ginti = 0;
function badhao() { ginti++; dikhao(); }
function ghatao() { ginti--; dikhao(); }
function dikhao() { document.getElementById("ginti").innerText = ginti; }
</script>
```

Input ka type password se text karne par akshar dikhne lagte hain. Har login page par ye chhota feature hota hai.

```html
<input type="password" id="pass">
<button onclick="dikhao()">Dikhao</button>
<script>
function dikhao() {
  let p = document.getElementById("pass");
  if (p.type === "password") {
    p.type = "text";
  } else {
    p.type = "password";
  }
}
</script>
```

Photos array me rakho aur number (index) badhate jao. Aakhri ke baad wapas 0 — isiliye slider gol ghumta rehta hai.

```html
<img id="photo" src="1.jpg" width="250">
<button onclick="agla()">Agla</button>
<script>
let photos = ["1.jpg", "2.jpg", "3.jpg"];
let i = 0;
function agla() {
  i++;
  if (i >= photos.length) i = 0;
  document.getElementById("photo").src = photos[i];
}
</script>
```

setItem se rakho, getItem se nikalo. Page band karke kholne par bhi data rehta hai — browser ke andar ki chhoti tijori hai.

```javascript
localStorage.setItem("naam", "Vishesh");
let rakha = localStorage.getItem("naam");
console.log(rakha);
```

JSON.stringify object ko bhej ne layak text bana deta hai. Server par data bhejna ho to pehle yahi hota hai. Ulta kaam JSON.parse karta hai.

```javascript
let student = { naam: "Amit", umar: 20 };
let text = JSON.stringify(student);
console.log(text);
```

Arrow function chhota roop hai — function shabd ki jagah => teer. Ek line ke chhote kaamo me ye har jagah dikhega. Jawab 12.

```javascript
let jod = (a, b) => a + b;
console.log(jod(5, 7));
```

setTimeout kaam ko taal deta hai — dusra number milliseconds me hai (2000 = 2 second). Pehla message turant, dusra 2 second baad aayega.

```javascript
console.log("Ruko...");
setTimeout(function() {
  console.log("2 second ho gaye!");
}, 2000);
```

typeof batata hai cheez kis prakar ki hai — number, string ya boolean. Jawab kram se number, string, boolean aayega.

```javascript
console.log(typeof 42);
console.log(typeof "namaste");
console.log(typeof true);
```

Class ke liye dot (.) aur id ke liye hash (#) — ulta kar doge to style lagegi hi nahi, aur koi galti (error) bhi nahi dikhegi.

```css
/* galat — note class hai, hash laga diya */
#note { color: red; }

/* sahi */
.note { color: red; }
```

Style na lage to sabse pehle yahi jaancho ki HTML me class hai ya id, aur CSS me waisa hi chinh hai.

jQuery ek purani JavaScript library hai jo lambe JS code ko chhota kar deti thi:

```javascript
// aam JS
document.getElementById("btn").style.color = "red";

// jQuery
$("#btn").css("color", "red");
```

Aaj kal naye browser khud itne achhe ho gaye hain ki naye project me jQuery kam use hoti hai — par purani sites par ye bahut milti hai, isliye pehchanna zaroori hai.
